**POST /api/v1/memos**

The mapping is declared as a `google.api.http` annotation on the RPC in `proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto:21-25`:

```proto
rpc CreateMemo(CreateMemoRequest) returns (Memo) {
  option (google.api.http) = {
    post: "/api/v1/memos"
    body: "memo"
  };
  option (google.api.method_signature) = "memo";
}
```

Two details worth noting alongside the path:
- `body: "memo"` — the HTTP request body is the `Memo` message itself, not the wrapping `CreateMemoRequest`. The optional `memo_id` field (`proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto:299`) therefore travels as a query parameter, not in the body.
- The server-side implementation behind this route is `APIV1Service.CreateMemo` at `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:70`, with the Connect handler adapter at `server/router/api/v1/connect_services.go:306`.
